{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nRewritten after premise refutation (see comments): the observed fold-horizon race (bridge write + concurrent compact → union merge lands an event timestamped before the snapshot, absent from `source_event_uuids`) is the known RC2 class of ADR-0035, and the repair door EXISTS and works: `rebar fsck --repair-snapshots` / `fsck --repair` → `compact.rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` (full HLC-ordered log incl. `.retired`, `.snapshot-rebuild.bak` sentinel, fail-closed guard) — it healed the live incident on e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2.\n\nThe REAL defect (verified in a RED run against current main): **the next natural fold LAUNDERS the orphan.** When a ticket with an un-cited pre-snapshot event crosses the compaction threshold, the fold's whole-dir enumeration RETIRES the orphan file and CITES its uuid in the new snapshot's `source_event_uuids` — but the replay's positional skip means its effect is NOT in the compiled state. fsck then reports clean (uuid cited, file retired): repairable damage silently becomes unrepairable-by-tooling loss at the first threshold crossing after the race. The existing repair door only works in the window BEFORE that fold. Secondary gaps: (G2) `doctor --repair` does not route ORPHAN_EVENT findings to the heal — only the fsck flags reach it; (G4) `fsck --repair-snapshots` rebuilds on ANY orphan type, bypassing the `_AUTO_RECOVER` vs `_HUMAN_TRIAGE` routing that `fsck --repair` enforces (fsck_repair.py:33-57).\n\n## Proposed fix\n1. **Stop the laundering (G1, the bug):** the natural fold (compact_txn) must EXCLUDE un-cited pre-snapshot events from both retirement and `source_event_uuids` citation — an orphan stays an unretired, un-cited file, so the fsck ORPHAN_EVENT finding and the repair window survive indefinitely. The fold does NOT absorb orphans itself (that would bypass the type routing); it defers to the repair door. Ordering note: `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` replays the full log in HLC total order, so absorbed order-sensitive events are deterministic there — no new ordering semantics are introduced by this change.\n2. **Doctor routing (G2):** `rebar doctor --repair` routes ORPHAN_EVENT findings through the same type-routed repair as `fsck --repair` (commutative types auto-heal via full-log rebuild; order-sensitive types surface as manual with the existing triage messaging), under the store write lock with the established backup envelope.\n3. **Routing parity (G4):** `--repair-snapshots` applies the same `_AUTO_RECOVER`/`_HUMAN_TRIAGE` routing instead of rebuilding unconditionally, so the two fsck repair paths cannot disagree about order-sensitive orphans.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py — fold enumeration excludes un-cited pre-snapshot events from retirement + citation (defer guard).\n- src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py — ORPHAN_EVENT repair routing (extends the merged 1771 repair table).\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py — routing parity for --repair-snapshots.\n- tests/unit/test_fold_orphan_laundering.py — new: RED reproduction of the laundering (orphan retired+cited+effect-lost today), exclusion behavior, repair-window survival across a threshold-crossing fold.\n- tests/unit/test_doctor_orphan_repair.py — new: doctor routing, type-split (COMMENT auto-heals; STATUS surfaces manual), backup envelope.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A ticket with an un-cited pre-snapshot COMMENT that crosses the compaction threshold keeps the orphan unretired/un-cited and fsck still reports ORPHAN_EVENT after the fold; `fsck --repair-snapshots` afterward restores the comment to `show`; integration test.\n- [ ] `rebar doctor --repair` heals a commutative orphan via full-log rebuild and surfaces an order-sensitive orphan as manual; unit tests.\n- [ ] `--repair-snapshots` no longer rebuilds past `_HUMAN_TRIAGE` types; guard test.\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nWriter-path auto-detection after union merge (G3 — separate follow-up if wanted); bridge/Jira duplicate policy; crash-atomicity (mantis, landed); dirty-tree repair (dormouse, landed).","title":"Natural fold launders ORPHAN_EVENTs (retires + cites without applying) — repairable race damage becomes silent loss; doctor lacks orphan routing"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786724638448315001,"uuid":"b18b29ff-f14a-44c9-a777-2d230e2f680d"}